<title>CANADA: Canada's Prairies to see rain west, sun east.</title>
<headline>Canada's Prairies to see rain west, sun east.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's Prairies on Thursday were forecast to see rain west, sun in the east, Environment Canada said.</p>
<p>Alberta should see rain in the south and central regions with highs of 15 to 23 Celsius.</p>
<p>Saskatchewan should see sunny skies with highs of 14 to 24 Celsius.</p>
<p>Manitoba should see sunny skies with highs of 23 to 26 Celsius.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras, Winnipeg Reuters bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
